# Finishing a craft at the bench.
#
# You've rolled a Rare ring you're happy with — a life prefix and two of the three
# suffixes you want — leaving one open suffix slot. Rather than gamble an Exalted
# Orb on hitting the last resistance, the crafting bench adds a *guaranteed*
# modifier into that slot: here, a cold resistance.
#
# The checker proves TWO preconditions for the bench craft:
#   - an open slot in the mod's generation (cold resistance is a suffix, and one
#     suffix slot is free) — fill all three suffixes and it errors instead; and
#   - no group conflict: the item mustn't already carry a mod of that group. Cold
#     resistance is a new group here; benching "fire resistance" instead would be
#     rejected, since this ring already has one (an item holds one mod per group).

craft in poe1

item {
    base:     "Iron Ring"
    ilvl:     84
    rarity:   rare
    prefixes: [ "maximum life" t2 ]
    suffixes: [ "fire resistance" t3, "lightning resistance" t3 ]
}

bench "cold resistance"
